-- title:
--   Thomson $N=7$, Case 1: precomputed Kronecker statistics, part 1 of 3
-- statement:
--   In H. Tran's proof of the Thomson problem for seven electrons, the polynomial identity of the Case 1 certificate is checked by a Kronecker substitution: each of the 13 pieces of the identity expression (the minorant part $H$, the four kernel blocks $F_0,\dots,F_3$ and the eight sum-of-squares blocks $S_0,\dots,S_7$) is mapped to a tuple of statistics $(\ell^1\text{-norm},\deg_u,\deg_v,\deg_t,\text{Kronecker value})$ with $w=179$, $D=11$.
--
--   This file records, as plain data, the precomputed tuples for the pieces H, F0, F1, F2. They are not trusted: the solution of the Case 1 lemma proves, by kernel evaluation, that each piece's statistics equal these values before using them.
--
--   **Formalization Note** In the source file these tuples appear as the right-hand sides of the theorems `c1_stat_*`; they are moved into definitions (with the large integers written in hexadecimal) only because of the platform's limits on submitted files.
-- source:
--   H. Tran, Thomson problem N = 7 Lean proof package (snapshot 2026-09-27), https://github.com/huwngtran/thomson-n7-lean @ 25f2fa53119273458cfbb3c4230904bffdd61e53, formal/lean/ThomsonN7/Solution.lean, Case 1 theorems `c1_stat_H` … `c1_stat_S7` (around lines 10380–10420)

